title: Walk_GregoryOfNyssa_Heim
tags: walk
speaker: Gregory
---
Gregory: God created the cosmos from nothing, giving it form and real presence.
Gregory: All created reality reflects the wisdom and purpose of its divine Author.
Gregory: Now our path leads deeper through the Metaphysics grove.
Gregory: Listen to the gentle rustle of leaves as we walk along this trail.
Gregory: We move from divine creation to human digital invention.
Gregory: Michael Heim waits in the clearing ahead.
Gregory: He asks whether worlds we build are real. Made in God's image, we too make.
Gregory: Consider whether software constructs possess authentic being or secondary artifice.
Gregory: Can digital creations share in real existence alongside physical nature?
Gregory: Let us approach his clearing and examine his virtual realism.
===
